{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '500,555p' src/flask/sansio/app.py; grep -RIn --include='*.py' 'select_jinja_autoescape' tests src; find tests -maxdepth 2 -type f -name '*templ*' -print; keelson new autoescape-extension-case --tier quick --touches 'src/flask/sansio/app.py,tests/test_templating.py' && keelson context --paths src/flask/sansio/app.py tests/test_templating.py && keelson impact src/flask/sansio/app.py tests/test_templating.py\"","aggregated_output":"✓ created .keelson/changes/autoescape-extension-case (quick, owner node, branch HEAD)\n· session focus → autoescape-extension-case\n· fill change.md acceptance; tasks.md is optional for a quick change\n# Keelson context — workspace\n\n## INTENT.md\n\n# workspace\n\n## Why this exists\nOne paragraph. The problem this project solves and for whom. If this paragraph is wrong, everything built on it is wrong.\n\n## Boundaries\n- In scope: …\n- Explicitly not: … (write the tempting things you have decided not to do)\n\n## Hard constraints\n- … (runtime, compatibility, performance, security, licensing)\n\n## Authorizations\nWhat the agent may decide alone, and what it must bring back with a recommendation.\n- Decides alone: local implementation choices inside a confirmed scope; test structure; naming that follows existing patterns.\n- Recommends, owner decides: anything that changes user-visible behaviour, scope, or a long-term commitment; new dependencies; public interface changes.\n- Always confirms: irreversible data operations, production changes, permission widening, breaking compatibility.\n\n## Working defaults\n- Change sizing: auto (the agent decides; override per request with \"treat as spec\" / \"just do it\")\n- Quick changes: proceed after write-back\n- Spec changes: wait for approval\n\n## NOW.md\n\n# Now\n\nFirst contact with workspace: Keelson was just initialised. Project intent will be derived from repository evidence as pa